      en: "Nyen Town is a settlement in Grand Gedeh County, Liberia, founded in the 1970s by Krahn refugees. Named after the Nyen River, the settlement consists of hastily built mud and corrugated iron houses. The community relies on subsistence farming and cross-border trade with Côte d'Ivoire. The town has a primary school, a health post with a nurse, and a small market. The population is estimated at 1,200. There is no electricity; generators are used by a few shops. The nearest urban center is Zwedru, 60 km away.",
